    "narrative": "The **Zurich Zebras** offensive output today is anchored by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13), who draws an elite matchup against Michael Lorenzen. His combination of a favorable hitter\u2019s park and the projected lead-off spot creates an optimal environment for speed-driven production, a key priority given our roster\u2019s focus on the stolen base category. **Trea Turner** (77.18) and **Kyle Schwarber** (76.47) provide the next tier of production, both benefiting significantly from a soft matchup against Max Scherzer, whose 5.32 xERA suggests a prime opportunity to drive up our R and RBI totals. While **Yordan Alvarez** (51.49) faces a tougher test against the southpaw Reid Detmers, his elite 0.452 xwOBA keeps him as a viable start despite the platoon disadvantage.\n\nStrategically, the optimizer favored **Christian Yelich** (60.26) for his high-efficiency platoon advantage against Jack Perkins, while **Luke Raley** (64.85) remains a standout play due to a potent combination of a high-ceiling park and a vulnerable arm in Brandon Young. The most difficult personnel decision involved **Lars Nootbaar** (50.86), who narrowly missed the starting lineup; despite his elite 0.406 xwOBA, the combination of a 41% rain risk and the lower projected efficiency compared to **Junior Caminero** (68.21) effectively pushed him to the bench to preserve our game caps. Owners should monitor the weather in the **Carson Benge** (57.88) game, as the rain risk is identical to that of **Lars Nootbaar** and **Nelson Velazquez**, potentially complicating our late-afternoon rotation if delays occur.",
